tus: ppublish\n\nJournal abbreviation: J Antibiot (Tokyo)\n\nJournal country: England\n\nJournal NLM unique ID: 0151115\n\nJournal linking ISSN: 0021-8820\n\nISSN: 0021-8820\n\nVolume: 12\n\nIssue: 2\n\nPages: 59-64\n\n## Authors\n\n  * A MIYAKE\n  * H IWASAKI\n  * T TAKEWAKA\n\n## Languages\n\n  * eng\n\n## Publication types\n\n  * Journal Article\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n  * Anti-Bacterial Agents\n  * Streptomyces / metabolism\n\n## Keywords\n\n  * ANTIBIOTICS/preparation of\n  * STREPTOMYCES/metabolism\n\n## Substances\n\n  * Anti-Bacterial Agents--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProduction of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/13286189/)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\n. 1955 Aug;8(4):105-9.\n\n# Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\nT OSATO, M UEDA, S FUKUYAMA, K YAGISHITA, Y OKAMI, H UMEZAWA\n\n  * PMID: 13286189\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\nT OSATO et al. J Antibiot (Tokyo). 1955 Aug.\n\n\n. 1955 Aug;8(4):105-9.\n\n### Authors\n\nT OSATO, M UEDA, S FUKUYAMA, K YAGISHITA, Y OKAMI, H UMEZAWA\n\n  * PMID: 13286189\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nCite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\nNo abstract available\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n  * [Button: Anti-Bacterial Agents* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Nitroimidazoles* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Streptomyces* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n## Substances\n\n  * [Button: Anti-Bacterial Agents ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Nitroimidazoles ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: azomycin ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nα-Rubromycin (Collinomycin) | Antibiotic | MedChemExpress (https://www.medchemexpress.com/alpha-rubromycin.html)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; α-Rubromycin (Collinomycin) is an antibiotic isolated from the mycelia of Streptomyces collinus. α-Rubromycin also acts as a DNA polymerase inhibitor, with an IC_{50} of 0.91 μM against bovine mammalian DNA polymerase. α-Rubromycin binds to the active region of DNA polymerase β, competes with nucleotide substrates for binding, and interferes with template-DNA interactions. α-Rubromycin inhibits the activities of telomerase, retroviral reverse transcriptase and terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase, as well as the growth of Staphylococcus aureus. α-Rubromycin can be used in studies related to bacterial infections.\n\nCat. No.: HY-119787\n\n# α-Rubromycin\n\n(Synonyms: Collinomycin)\n\nα-Rubromycin (Collinomycin) is an antibiotic isolated from the mycelia of Streptomyces collinus. α-Rubromycin also acts as a DNA polymerase inhibitor, with an IC_{50} of 0.91 μM against bovine mammalian DNA polymerase. α-Rubromycin binds to the active region of DNA polymerase β, competes with nucleotide substrates for binding, and interferes with template-DNA interactions. α-Rubromycin inhibits the activities of telomerase, retroviral reverse transcriptase and terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase, as well as the growth of Staphylococcus aureus. α-Rubromycin can be used in studies related to bacterial infections.\n\nFor research use only. We do not sell to patients.\n\n  * CAS No.: 27267-69-2\n  * Formula: C_{27}H_{20}O_{12}\n  * Molecular Weight:536.44\n\n  * Sto